From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:46:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: dcp: let the T8132 HDMI output's idle
 release engage

hdmi_idle_release is meant to let an idle T8132 HDMI output release its
DisplayPort-only PHY and crossbar output, but it never did anything.
dcp_fabric_hdmi_park() returned unless dcp->external_native was set,
and that flag is only set for a T6030 external display processor
(dcp_t6030_ext_native()). The park is only ever called for a T8132
dcpext, from its idle work, so the check stopped every call. Check for
a T8132 dcpext instead.

The output was also taken back only from the HPD interrupt thread. The
HDMI recheck work acts on the HPD level too, and could have connected
a display on a released output. Take the PHY and crossbar back at the
start of dcp_hdmi_update_locked(), which every HDMI update goes
through, under the same fabric lock.

The switch stays off by default.

Fixes: 3c5cb5334880 ("drm: apple: dcp: let an idle T8132 HDMI output release its PHY and crossbar")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 7c2c90fd58274b29401bf86f1ce8ec40cd59ffbe)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c
index df50599c70..3342590e61 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c
@@ -1360,7 +1360,7 @@ void dcp_fabric_hdmi_park(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	guard(mutex)(&dcp_typec_fabric_lock);
-	if (!dcp->external_native || !dcp->fixed_phy || !dcp->hdmi_hpd || dcp->hdmi_parked)
+	if (!dcp_is_t8132_ext(dcp) || !dcp->fixed_phy || !dcp->hdmi_hpd || dcp->hdmi_parked)
 		return;
 	if (dcp->active_typec_route || gpiod_get_value_cansleep(dcp->hdmi_hpd) > 0)
 		return;
@@ -5298,6 +5298,9 @@ static void dcp_hdmi_update_locked(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 	int level;
 
 	lockdep_assert_held(&dcp_typec_fabric_lock);
+	/* A display on a released output: take the PHY and crossbar back first. */
+	if (dcp->hdmi_parked && gpiod_get_value_cansleep(dcp->hdmi_hpd) > 0)
+		dcp_fixed_hdmi_unpark_locked(dcp);
 	if (dcp_hdmi_settle_enabled(dcp)) {
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&dcp->hdmi_presence_lock, flags);
 		generation = dcp->hdmi_presence.generation;
@@ -5323,9 +5326,6 @@ irqreturn_t dcp_dp2hdmi_hpd(int irq, void *data)
 void dcp_fabric_hdmi_sample(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 {
 	guard(mutex)(&dcp_typec_fabric_lock);
-	if (dcp->hdmi_parked && dcp->hdmi_hpd &&
-	    gpiod_get_value_cansleep(dcp->hdmi_hpd) > 0)
-		dcp_fixed_hdmi_unpark_locked(dcp);
 	dcp_hdmi_update_locked(dcp);
 	/* Attached or not may have changed. */
 	dcp_t8132_idle_kick(dcp);
